.TH NXVIEW 1
.SH NAME
nxview \- graphical image viewer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nxview
[file ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
View local PNG, baseline JPEG, GIF or BMP files in a resizable Nano-X window.
GIF displays its first frame. Transparent images appear over a checkerboard.
With no arguments, a file selector opens. Opening another file or cancelling
the selector preserves the current picture until a replacement loads successfully.
Files are decoded by the shared image library, independently of NetSurf.
.SH CONTROLS
Open or O/Ctrl-O opens the file selector. F or 0 fits the picture into the
window without enlarging small pictures. 1 selects actual size.
+ and - zoom around the centre of the visible picture, from 10% to 800%
subject to coordinate limits. Drag the picture or use arrow keys to pan;
the mouse wheel pans vertically. [ and ] or PageUp/PageDown select the
previous/next filename supplied on the command line. Q or Escape closes
the viewer. The toolbar provides equivalent open, previous/next, fit,
actual-size and zoom controls.
.SH LIMITS
Files must be regular files of at most 1 MiB, with at most 262144 pixels
and no dimension greater than 4096 pixels. Unsupported or damaged files
report an error in the status bar and on standard error. Progressive JPEG,
animation, SVG, remote URLs, editing and saving conversions are not supported.
Available process memory may impose a lower limit, particularly on RVM.
.SH EXAMPLE
nxview /usr/share/netsurf/images/landscape.jpg
